WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.338
Now a physical product.

2
00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:10.619
I ask my agent for an LED desk lamp under ninety dollars with tracked delivery.

3
00:00:10.619 --> 00:00:13.160
My spending mandate is already active.

4
00:00:14.526 --> 00:00:17.870
The agent searches real products through Channel3.

5
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.946
Only the words LED desk lamp leave the system.

6
00:00:20.946 --> 00:00:26.430
Every listing is screened as untrusted data, and anything over budget is excluded.

7
00:00:27.543 --> 00:00:33.807
It picks the cheapest eligible real listing and negotiates a delivered price with three reseller agents.

8
00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:41.393
The contract binds the exact listing, the retailer, the price, the delivery address and the carrier.

9
00:00:42.494 --> 00:00:43.588
No click from me.

10
00:00:43.588 --> 00:00:49.766
The purchase fits my mandate, so the agent signs it, and PayPal authorizes from my saved wallet.

11
00:00:50.885 --> 00:00:52.014
The reseller ships.

12
00:00:52.014 --> 00:00:58.013
QuarantinePay doesn't take the seller's word for it: it needs a delivery proof signed by the carrier.

13
00:00:58.978 --> 00:01:05.410
The carrier's signature, the order, the item, the address and the delivered status all check out.

14
00:01:06.515 --> 00:01:10.811
So the payment is captured automatically, and PayPal confirms it.

15
00:01:11.931 --> 00:01:16.731
On the next order, the seller claims delivery with a proof it signed itself.

16
00:01:17.684 --> 00:01:19.721
The carrier signature fails.

17
00:01:19.721 --> 00:01:24.812
Nothing is captured: the hold is voided, and PayPal confirms the void.

18
00:01:25.931 --> 00:01:30.007
Real products, autonomous buying, independent verification.

19
00:01:30.007 --> 00:01:33.875
Agents decide, and PayPal pays only for what was proven.
